@translation labeled en project










@h1 Version A

@(1.1 = 1-7) Say this to the king who like the sun has made the heart of the Land radiant. Repeat it to the one who removed oppressive toil from the furrow, who @varh[t3303.1.v1]{defeated } @vart[t3303.1.v2,t3303.1.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} confronted }  @wEN{Tidnum} and holds its sceptre, who is counted as its honoured king. This is what @varh[t3303.1.v3]{@wPN{Lugal-nesaŋe} } @vart[t3303.1.v4,t3303.1.v3]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} @wPN{Lugal-šu} } , a citizen of @wSN{Nibru} and your servant, says:

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3303.1.v1 t3303.1.v2
#etcsl#alt t3303.1.v3 t3303.1.v4
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(1.8 = 8-15) A punishment which I do not understand has ravaged me and I have wailed my lamenting. In a strange city I moan like a dove and receive no mercy. I am constantly restless like a dog which does not know where to settle down. I am watchful like a bird which has flown from the claws of a falcon. My exuberance has perished in blight like a garden that has not been @varh[t3303.1.v5]{watered } @vart[t3303.1.v6,t3303.1.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} tended } . Envy within my king's palace overwhelms me and a bad reputation besets me.

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3303.1.v5 t3303.1.v6
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(1.16 = 16-31) Grief ……. Woe ……. Like an ox I am overwhelmed, …… my fodder. My descendants and offspring are on good terms …… their nest, …… the mouth for eating food. @varh[t3303.1.v7]{As happens on } @vart[t3303.1.v8,t3303.1.v7]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} Like a distant …… from }  the …… high plains where the winds blow, …… the mill. I will not be buried on dying but …… ground like grain. My brother, although not an enemy, …… contemptuously.

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3303.1.v7 t3303.1.v8
#etcsl#altGrpc

$ (approx. 6 lines missing)
$ (3 lines fragmentary)
@(1.32 = 32-33) The king ……, …… like @wDN{Utu}.





@h1 Version B (from Kiš)

$ (unknown no. of lines missing)
@(2.1 = 1-9) …… a bird …… the claws of a falcon. …… like a garden which has been watered. Envy within my king's palace overwhelms me and ……. Grief ……. Woe ……. Like an ox I am overwhelmed, like …… my fodder. My descendants and offspring are worried in their nests. Like a distant …… from the …… high plains where the winds blow, …… the mill. I will not experience being buried as befits the dead but …… ground like grain.

$ (unknown no. of lines missing)




